[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"160","stub":{"id":"160","section":"Los Padres Reservoir to Carmel Valley","altname":"","river":"Carmel","difficulty":"IItoIII","states":["USA-CAL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"37","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"Located near the base of the old Los Padres Dam.","id":"112892","location":{"latitude":"36.388109","longitude":"-121.667513"},"name":"Cachagua County Park Put-In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"other","description":"In the summer of 2015, after years of planning and three years of de-construction, the 95 year-old and 106 foot tall San Clemente Dam was removed on the Carmel River. The dam would have required extensive upgrades to meet earthquake safety standards which would have cost in the range of $55 million. At the time, San Clemente Dam removal was the largest dam removal project in California. Once blocked and disconnected, the Carmel River is now free-flowing allowing steelhead to access over 25 miles of spawning and rearing habitat upstream, letting sediment travel downstream to naturally replenish Carmel River beach, and resolving public safety issues associated with San Clemente Dam. A rapid is now present at the former dam site.","id":"kRZ1qMiFVzZfh84UUgcwn","location":{"latitude":"36.436194","longitude":"-121.708547"},"name":"San Clemente Dam Site","distance":"6.91","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"118171","location":{"latitude":"36.474428","longitude":"-121.728429"},"name":"Carmel Valley Take-Out","distance":"11.23","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"3","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"2390","description":"","caption":"Carmel River","poi_name":"","subject":"Bob lifting off","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3"}}],"detail":{"id":"160","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"If you're willing to put up with some shallow portages around wood, this can be a fun overnight (combined with the downstream portion to the mouth) or a daytrip. Class II with a Class III rapid at the old dam site, with steelhead aplenty (thanks to that dam being removed).\n\n**Other Information Sources:**\n\n[California Creekin](http://cacreeks.com/carmel3.htm)\n\n[Carmel River Watershed Conservancy](http://www.carmelriverwatershed.org/)\n\n[Carmel River Steelhead Association](http://www.carmelriversteelheadassociation.org/)\n\n[The Loma Prieta Paddlers](http://lomaprietapaddlers.org/) club is centered in the San Jose area, but they have members in the Santa Cruz and Monterey/Carmel area.","averageGradient":"60","maxGradient":null,"length":"11","correlations":[{"reachID":"160","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"250","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"750"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"CARMEL R A ROBLES DEL RIO CA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"11143200","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"37","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"2.36","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"36.4748611","longitude":"-121.7288889"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/11143200","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-loca